
-> What is JIT Compiler?

Just-In-Time Compiler
    Converts bytecode to machine code at runtime
    Stores optimized code for reuse

Interpreter vs JIT
    | Interpreter     | JIT                   |
    | --------------- | --------------------- |
    | Line by line    | Compiles whole method |
    | Slow            | Fast                  |
    | No optimization | Optimized code        |

Why JIT is Important?
    Improves performance
    Reduces repeated interpretation
    Makes Java fast like native languages